/* The verify-email banner's wash (components/nx/Banners.tsx's shared `Banner`).
   Dark mode is the exact gradient that lived inline before this moved to a
   class — weighted to the accent on the left where the icon sits, fading to a
   near-solid dark tail on the right. Light mode fades to near-white instead of
   dark navy, so the banner reads as a tinted notice on the page it is
   actually sitting on rather than a dark island the light theme forgot.
   `--banner-rgb` is set per-instance (Banners.tsx), so this stays reusable for
   any accent color, not just the amber verify-email uses today. */
.nx-banner-wash {
  background: linear-gradient(96deg, rgba(var(--banner-rgb), 0.13), rgba(var(--banner-rgb), 0.05) 38%, rgba(1, 15, 34, 0.86));
}
