/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   NEXION component layer, brought over from the design sandbox.

   Nested under `:root:has(.nx-shell-root)`, not applied bare — this whole
   layer redefines shared class names (.card, .glass, .btn, .btn-primary,
   .btn-ghost, .field — the same names the marketing site, login/register
   and the admin portal already use with their OWN, production-original
   rules). Before this was scoped, "appended after the original layer"
   meant it won EVERYWHERE by cascade order, including on marketing/login/
   admin — exactly the "buttons look different on the marketing site" bug
