   because several dashboard modals `createPortal` to `document.body`,
   landing as DOM siblings of `.nx-shell-root` rather than descendants —
   only `:root:has(...)` reaches those too. `.label` was renamed
   `.nx-label` — the original is a form label used across the app.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
@layer components {
  :root:has(.nx-shell-root) {
  /* ── Overrides of block-1 shared classes, scoped to the portal ──────────
     These used to be bare rules in the layer above, winning everywhere
     (marketing/login/admin included) purely by appearing later in the file.
     Moved here, under the has() scope, so production's own .card/.glass/
     .btn-* definitions above are what marketing/login/admin actually get. */
  @property --nx-btn-spin {
